235
00:12:37,919 --> 00:12:39,759
No, no.

236
00:12:40,039 --> 00:12:41,559
Moved to a tall tree,

237
00:12:42,519 --> 00:12:43,600
could it be...

238
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:45,960
Is it the character for "bridge"?

239
00:12:48,679 --> 00:12:50,720
"Bridge": wood left, Qiao right.

240
00:12:51,399 --> 00:12:52,799
The top is concave, forming the shape of a curve.

241
00:12:53,159 --> 00:12:54,240
It's called wood above the curve.

242
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,519
Moving to the tall tree is the key to the riddle.

243
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,159
Moving the tall tree and the wood together makes a bridge.

244
00:12:59,559 --> 00:13:00,399
There is no bridge over the water.

245
00:13:01,039 --> 00:13:02,480
It's hard for pedestrians to pass.

246
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,240
Good.

247
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:04,639
Good.

248
00:13:07,639 --> 00:13:08,080
Come on.

249
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:11,679
Congratulations to this young man.

250
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,440
You guessed it too quickly.

251
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,960
Because I also have a bridge in my heart.

252
00:13:22,879 --> 00:13:23,879
There is a Qingqiao in my heart.

253
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,360
It cannot be turned.

254
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:31,080
Come on.

255
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,440
On the west side of Qingqiao,

256
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:34,320
